>> title: Gỏi Cuốn
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: pork, shrimp, vietnamese, no-cook, rice paper
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: goi cuon, gỏi cuốn, fresh spring rolls, spring rolls, summer rolls, salad rolls, rice paper rolls, cold rolls, A2
>> pairs-with: nuoc-cham
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min

>> step: poach 12 min, cool and slice
Poach @pork belly{8%oz}(225 g; in one piece) and @shrimp{16%large}(450 g; shell on) in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} ~poach{12%min}, the shrimp out at three minutes and the pork at twelve, then slice the pork thin and split each shrimp.

>> step: boil 4 min, rinse cold
Boil @rice vermicelli{4%oz}(115 g) in @hot water{2%qt}(1.9 L) ~boil{4%min}, then drain and rinse cold so the strands stop sticking to each other.

>> step: soften, fill and roll tight
Soften @rice paper wrappers{12} one at a time in @warm water{1%qt}(950 mL), lay @&(~1)noodles{} and @&(~2)pork and shrimp{} across the near third with @lettuce{12%leaves}, @mint{1/2%cup} and @garlic chives{12}(left whole, sticking out one end), then roll tight, tucking the sides in on the second turn.

>> step: stir the peanut sauce
Stir @hoisin sauce{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @peanut butter{2%Tbs}(30 g), @warm water{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @roasted peanuts{2%Tbs}(chopped) into a dipping sauce loose enough to fall off a spoon.

>> step: arrange whole or halved, with the sauce
Arrange @&(~2)rolls{} whole, or halved on a sharp diagonal, alongside @&(~1)peanut sauce{}.
